        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Check if Input is Valid"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "true": "1765986087529",
            "false": "1766577144102"
          },
          "code": "CHECK_IF_INPUT_IS_VALID",
          "convergenceTargetId": "end",
          "id": "1759710535608",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759710535610_1",
              "name": "condition",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "{{$context.$nodes.VALIDATING_THE_INPUT.$output.Valid == true}}"
            }
          ],
          "type": "CONDITION"
        },
        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Validating the Input"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759710535608"
          },
          "code": "VALIDATING_THE_INPUT",
          "id": "1759710573008",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759710573008_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "Default variables (assume these are set before running):\n- userInput: {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n- promptMessage: ''\n\nTask: Validate the userInput against the rules below. Produce exactly one JSON object as output (no extra text). The JSON must contain:\n{\n  \"Valid\": true | false,\n  \"FailReason\": null | \"<short reason>\",\n  \"AttachmentPrompt\": null | \"<prompt message>\"\n}\n\nValidation rules (run in order):\n\n1) Empty Input Check  \n- Condition: userInput must not be empty, blank, or contain only whitespace.  \n- If this fails:  \n  - Output: {\"Valid\": false, \"FailReason\": \"The input is empty.\", \"AttachmentPrompt\": \"\"}  \n  - STOP  \n\n2) Final Decision\n- If all checks pass, \n  - Sub task is to read `userInput` and understand the customer’s reported problem.\n  - Based on this message, define a prompt that can identify what specific information should be looked for inside the attachment.\n\n    What you must do:\n    - Do not analyze any attachment yet — only define what needs to be searched for later.\n    - Extract the key issue(s) the customer is reporting.\n    - Identify what kinds of data, errors, or evidence the attachment should contain to help diagnose the issue.\n    - With all the details generate a short prompt and store in `promptMessage`\n    - Do not describe the prompt, the prompt should have the exact information to search in attachment.\n    - Do not include any special characters.\n    - Limit the prompt to 100-200 characters.\n    - If the `userInput` is not clear then set `promptMessage` to \"Get the summary of the attachment\"\n    - Output: {\"Valid\": true, \"FailReason\": null, \"AttachmentPrompt\": `promptMessage`}\n\nAdditional instructions:  \n- Do not add any commentary or explanation. Output exactly the JSON object and nothing else.  \n- Use exact FailReason labels:  \n  - \"The input is empty.\""
            },
            {
              "id": "1759710573009_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"FailReason\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        },\n        \"Valid\": {\n            \"type\": \"boolean\"\n        },\n       \"AttachmentPrompt\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
        {
