        {
          "metadata": {
            "name": "Determine Severity"
          },
          "outcomes": {
            "success": "1759729348202"
          },
          "code": "DETERMINE_SEVERITY",
          "id": "1759729310063",
          "inputs": [
            {
              "id": "1759729310064_1",
              "name": "prompt",
              "type": "string",
              "value": "You are an AI assistant responsible for classifying the **severity** of a problem based on the provided description and mapping it to the correct lookup code.  \nYour output **must only be in JSON format** — no explanations, no extra text.  \n\n---\n\n## Step 1: Classify Severity\nDetermine the severity level from the {{$context.$variables.ProblemDescription}} using these rules:  \n\n- **Low** → Minor inconvenience, no immediate impact, workaround available.  \n- **Medium** → Noticeable disruption, affects user productivity, needs timely attention but not critical.  \n- **High** → Critical issue, major service/system impact, no workaround, requires urgent resolution.  \n\n---\n\n## Step 2: Use Lookup List\nYou will be given a list of items {{$context.$nodes.GET_SEVERITY_DETAILS.$output.items}} containing `Meaning` and `LookupCode` which matches Low, Medium and High.\n\n---\n\n## Step 3: Map Severity to Code\n- Match the classified severity (Low, Medium, High) with the corresponding `Meaning` in the list.  \n- Retrieve the associated `LookupCode`.  \n- Return the result strictly in the following JSON format:  \n\n```json\n{\n  \"Severity\": \"Low | Medium | High\",\n  \"SeverityCd\": \"<Matching LookupCode>\"\n}"
            },
            {
              "id": "1759729310064_2",
              "name": "temperature",
              "type": "number",
              "value": ""
            }
          ],
          "outputSpecification": "{\n    \"$schema\": \"http://json-schema.org/draft-04/schema#\",\n    \"type\": \"object\",\n    \"properties\": {\n        \"SeverityCd\": {\n            \"type\": \"string\"\n        }\n    }\n}",
          "type": "LLM"
        },
