              "value": "### Data\n`userInputMessage` = {{$context.$system.$inputMessage}}\n`outputLanguage` = \"English\"\n\n### Output Language\nAlways generate Title and ProblemDescription in the same language as `userInputMessage`. \nDo not assume the language.\n\n### Step 1: Detect Output Language (MANDATORY)\nIdentify the exact language of `userInputMessage`\nStore it as `outputLanguage`\n\nExamples:\nIf `userInputMessage` is English → `outputLanguage` = English\nIf Hindi → Hindi\nIf Spanish → Spanish\n\n### Global Language Constraint (STRICT)\nTitle and ProblemDescription outputs MUST be ONLY in `outputLanguage` language.\nDO NOT translate or switch language under any condition\nIf multiple languages are present, use the dominant language of `userInputMessage`\nIf validation fails, REGENERATE\n\n### Step 2: Generate `Title` (Max 400 characters)\nCraft a concise, informative title summarizing from `userInputMessage` in the requester’s own words, as if they wrote it themselves. \n- Do not write from the agent’s perspective.\n\n### Step 3: Create `ProblemDescription` (Max 700 characters)\n- Write a concise summary of the main issue.\n- Write a concise first person summary (I, my) of the main issue.\n- Do not state that I already performed troubleshooting. Instead, list the AI/agent guidance as suggested next steps (e.g., “Suggested: …”).\n- Do not state ticket or case identifiers and action request phrases (e.g., \"log a ticket,\" \"please raise a request\").\n- Use only the content from  `userInputMessage`.\n- Do not use any double quotes or single quotes.\n- Do not exceed 700 characters.\n- Final output of ProblemDescription should not exceeding 700 characters.\n\n### Step 4: Language Validation (CRITICAL)\nVerify Title and ProblemDescription are in `outputLanguage` language\nIf ANY word is from another language → REGENERATE\nDo NOT output mixed-language content\n\n### Step 5: Set Critical Flag (`CriticalFlag`)\n- Set to `true` if this issue has critical impact on the requester’s operations \n- Set to `false` if no"
